.TH TABLET 1 "2026-11-13" "tablet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tablet \- the VPN lamp for waybar, around openvpn3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tablet
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tablet
follows every openvpn3 session on the system bus and shows one lamp in a
waybar module: dim while nothing is connected, frost while a tunnel is held
and its checks pass, amber while it connects, waits on a sign\-in or an
agent's request, and red when it is stale, failed or dropped.
A held tunnel is checked: the hosts a profile names must answer, the
tunnel's DNS must have the profile's resolvers and zones, and the server
must keep sending.
A tunnel openvpn3 calls connected that fails those checks is
.IR stale .
.PP
Tablet does not speak the VPN protocol.
It starts sessions with
.BR "openvpn3 session\-start" ,
ends them over D\-Bus, and reads the rest.
It also watches openvpn3 itself: when an update removes a library an
openvpn3 build needs, the lamp says
.I rebuild
before you click it.
.PP
One binary is the daemon, the waybar module and the command line.
Commands start the daemon when it is not running.
Right\-clicking the module opens a drawer
.RB ( tablet\-board ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI connect " \fR[\fPprofile\fR]\fP"
Start a session for the profile, or the default profile.
A stale, failed or dropped profile is reconnected.
.TP
.BI disconnect " \fR[\fPprofile\fR|\fP\-\-all\fR]\fP"
End the profile's sessions, or every session Tablet sees with
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.BI reconnect " \fR[\fPprofile\fR]\fP"
End the profile's session and start a new one.
.TP
.B flip
What a left click on the lamp does: accept a waiting agent request, open a
waiting sign\-in page, connect the default profile when it is off,
disconnect it when it is held or connecting, reconnect it otherwise.
.TP
.BI ack " \fR[\fPprofile\fR]\fP"
Dismiss a dropped or failed profile; a failed session that lingers is
disconnected.
.TP
.BI signin " \fR[\fPprofile\fR]\fP"
Open the sign\-in page openvpn3 is waiting on again.
.TP
.BI check " \fR[\fPprofile\fR]\fP"
Check now and print each probe, the DNS and the traffic counters.
Exits 75 when a tunnel does not work.
.TP
.BI why " host\fR|\fPurl"
Say which profile a host needs (by the profiles'
.B zones
and
.B outside
lists) and whether it is up.
Exits 75 when the profile it needs is not held, so an agent can tell a
dropped tunnel from a broken service.
.TP
.BI need " \fR[\fPprofile\fR] [\fP\-\-reason text\fR] [\fP\-\-timeout secs\fR]\fP \-\- command\fR...\fP"
Run a command once the profile is connected.
When it is not, the lamp turns amber and the drawer shows the request,
the command, its directory and the reason; nothing connects until you
click Connect.
Exits 75 without running the command when you decline or nobody answers
within the timeout (300 seconds).
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
Every profile, any session no profile claims, waiting requests and
openvpn3's health.
.TP
.BR history " [" \-\-count
.IR n ]
What happened, newest first: connected, reconnected, stale, recovered,
failed, dropped, disconnected, broken, repaired.
.TP
.BR doctor " [" \-\-repair ]
Check the config, the profiles' files, openvpn3 and its libraries,
systemd\-resolved, the polkit rule, the daemon, the compositor and the
waybar config.
With
.B \-\-repair
run
.BR doctor.repair .
.TP
.BR toggle " [" \-\-center ]
Open or close the drawer from the clicked icon (for
.BR on\-click\-right ).
.TP
.BR show " [" \-\-center "], " hide
Open or close the drawer.
.TP
.B bar
The waybar module: prints a JSON line whenever the lamp changes.
Starts the daemon if it is not running.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground.
Exits 75 when another daemon is already running.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the daemon; the drawer starts on the next click.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH WAYBAR
.nf
"custom/tablet": {
  "exec": "tablet bar",
  "return-type": "json",
  "on-click": "tablet flip",
  "on-click-right": "tablet toggle",
  "on-click-middle": "tablet check"
}
.fi
.PP
Classes:
.BR off ", " held ", " degraded ", " connecting ", " signin ", " asking ,
.BR stale ", " failed ", " dropped ", " broken ", " offline ,
and
.B pulse
while it waits on something.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tablet/config.toml
Profiles and settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tablet/style.css
The drawer's style, over the theme taken from waybar.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablet/history.jsonl
What happened, one JSON object a line.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablet/daemon.log ", " board.log
Logs. Sign\-in URLs are never written to them.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tablet/tablet.sock
The daemon's socket.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR TABLET_CONFIG_DIR ", " TABLET_STATE_DIR ", " TABLET_RUNTIME_DIR
Move the config, the state and the socket, to run a second copy.
.TP
.B DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS
The bus openvpn3 is on.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, 75 when the VPN is the problem
.RB ( check ", " why ", " need )
or when a daemon is already running
.RB ( daemon ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openvpn3 (8),
.BR resolvectl (1),
.BR waybar (5)
